        "original_id": "451eac65-5eb3-5050-95de-0b222bfd48df",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lewis Carroll\n- Characters: Hatter, March Hare, Haigha, Mad Hatter\n- Works: Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, Through the Looking-Glass\n- Topics: fictional character adaptations, tea party scene\n\nFacts:\n- Lewis Carroll created the Hatter as a fictional character in \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.\"\n- Lewis Carroll included the Hatter again in the sequel \"Through the Looking-Glass.\"\n- Lewis Carroll featured the March Hare in the tea party scene in \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.\"\n- In \"Through the Looking-Glass,\" the March Hare is called Haigha.\n- The comics character Mad Hatter is modeled after the Hatter from Lewis Carroll's \"Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.\"\n- In adaptations of Lewis Carroll's works, the Hatter is often called the \"Mad Hatter.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
